Subject: makefile.com: compile with IEEE floating point on Alpha

VSI C on Alpha defaults to /FLOAT=G_FLOAT, unlike IA64 and x86-64 (IEEE).
make uses doubles only for the -l load limit and its parsing, but IEEE is
what the other VMS ports use.  Add /FLOAT=IEEE_FLOAT/IEEE_MODE=DENORM_RESULTS
on Alpha only (ARCH_NAME compared as an upper-case string with .EQS.).

--- a/makefile.com
+++ b/makefile.com
@@ -49,6 +49,10 @@
 $   endif
 $ endif
 $!
+$! VSI C on Alpha defaults to G_FLOAT doubles; IA64 and x86-64 are IEEE
+$! already.  Ask for IEEE T_float on Alpha, as the other ports do.
+$ if f$edit(f$getsyi("ARCH_NAME"),"UPCASE") .eqs. "ALPHA" -
+  then ccopt = ccopt + "/float=ieee_float/ieee_mode=denorm_results"
 $!
 $ if (p1 .eqs. "LIST")
 $ then
